1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,531
Every school observes lessons.

2
00:00:02,531 --> 00:00:05,384
Very few can show what happens next.

3
00:00:05,384 --> 00:00:13,129
This is the Observation System: one route from a single lesson, to evidence, to a plan for every teacher.

4
00:00:13,129 --> 00:00:15,167
Here is the whole journey.

5
00:00:15,617 --> 00:00:18,512
It starts in the classroom, on an iPad.

6
00:00:18,512 --> 00:00:20,321
The observer opens one form.

7
00:00:20,321 --> 00:00:31,176
Teacher, subject, class and timing come from live dropdowns, fed by the school's own staff directory, so nothing is typed from memory and no list is ever out of date.

8
00:00:31,176 --> 00:00:33,347
Class composition is a few taps.

9
00:00:33,347 --> 00:00:37,327
The whole context of the lesson, captured in under a minute.

10
00:00:37,777 --> 00:00:45,399
Judgements use the regulator's own six point scale, from Outstanding to Very Weak, with the same proportion bands inspectors already use.

11
00:00:45,399 --> 00:00:51,207
Ten criteria, from attainment and progress to teaching and leadership, each with room for a comment.

12
00:00:51,207 --> 00:00:55,925
The form speaks the language of inspection, because it was built from it.

13
00:00:56,375 --> 00:00:58,136
Real observation notes are handwritten.

14
00:00:58,136 --> 00:01:00,602
So the form has an Evidence Pad.

15
00:01:00,602 --> 00:01:12,579
The observer writes with Apple Pencil, keeps photos of the board or the pupils' work alongside, and the system reads the handwriting and types it into the right field, usually before the lesson ends.

16
00:01:12,579 --> 00:01:15,398
Transcription only, never judgement; the ratings stay human.

17
00:01:15,398 --> 00:01:18,568
And every stroke survives a closed lid, mid lesson.

18
00:01:19,019 --> 00:01:21,159
When it is done, Save and Lock.

19
00:01:21,159 --> 00:01:24,828
The record gets an ID, freezes, and can never be edited again.

20
00:01:24,828 --> 00:01:28,802
Three seconds later the form is clean and ready for the next lesson.

21
00:01:28,802 --> 00:01:33,694
Observers file back to back all morning; a full inspection week runs on this one screen.

22
00:01:34,143 --> 00:01:36,666
One tap files everything, four ways at once.

23
00:01:36,666 --> 00:01:39,819
The record lands in a spreadsheet the school already owns.

24
00:01:39,819 --> 00:01:42,973
It mirrors into a live database, duplicate proof by design.

25
00:01:42,973 --> 00:01:46,757
A branded backup email goes to leadership with the locked record link.

26
00:01:46,757 --> 00:01:49,595
And the handwriting itself is archived in private storage.

27
00:01:49,595 --> 00:01:51,802
If any step fails, it retries quietly.

28
00:01:51,802 --> 00:01:54,325
Nobody in a school ever sees an error.

29
00:01:54,776 --> 00:01:56,953
Now the other end of the pipeline.

30
00:01:56,953 --> 00:02:00,374
The dashboard opens with a password, because everything inside is real.

31
00:02:00,374 --> 00:02:03,172
As an example, here is one school's June round.

32
00:02:03,172 --> 00:02:09,392
The story plays itself: a hundred and eleven lessons, a hundred and five teachers, counted up live from the records.

33
00:02:09,392 --> 00:02:11,880
Where judgements sit on the six point scale.

34
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:12,812
What is working.

35
00:02:12,812 --> 00:02:14,056
Where to focus next.

36
00:02:14,056 --> 00:02:18,721
And one tap presents it full screen, built to run itself in a governors' meeting.

37
00:02:19,170 --> 00:02:21,356
Every written claim carries a small number.

38
00:02:21,356 --> 00:02:26,978
Open it, and there are the lessons behind the claim: subject, date, judgement, and the inspector's words, verbatim.

39
00:02:26,978 --> 00:02:29,789
Over six hundred references sit behind a single round.

40
00:02:29,789 --> 00:02:32,912
Nothing on this dashboard is an opinion without its evidence.

41
00:02:33,362 --> 00:02:34,611
Rounds compare shows movement.

42
00:02:34,611 --> 00:02:41,796
Every teacher seen in both rounds is a line, from where they were to where they are, green when they moved toward Outstanding.

43
00:02:41,796 --> 00:02:45,232
A transition matrix counts the improvements, the holds and the declines.

44
00:02:45,232 --> 00:02:48,668
This is the question governors actually ask: is teaching getting better?

45
00:02:48,668 --> 00:02:49,917
Answered from the records.

46
00:02:50,367 --> 00:02:53,176
Coverage answers the other question: who has been seen?

47
00:02:53,176 --> 00:03:00,044
Teachers on the register, teachers observed, lessons per teacher, and who is still waiting, so no one is invisible for a term.

48
00:03:00,494 --> 00:03:02,993
Drill into any teacher and the record follows.

49
00:03:02,993 --> 00:03:06,118
Two gauges, student progress and teaching, averaged across every observation.

50
00:03:06,118 --> 00:03:09,242
Each session, its skills and its notes, one card each.

51
00:03:09,242 --> 00:03:21,426
And below them, a coaching plan: drafted by AI from that teacher's own lessons, checked word for word against the source, grounded in the school's own rubric, and approved by a human coach before the teacher ever sees it.

52
00:03:21,876 --> 00:03:23,438
Teachers have their own door.

53
00:03:23,438 --> 00:03:29,684
A portal for every member of staff: their photograph, their record, and a notification when a new plan is approved.

54
00:03:29,684 --> 00:03:32,807
What they see is deliberately thinner than what leadership sees.

55
00:03:32,807 --> 00:03:38,116
No observer's rough notes, no other teachers, only their own approved record and their own next steps.

56
00:03:38,566 --> 00:03:48,743
For the leadership table, one button turns the round into a governance report, simple or in depth, and a second builds it as a branded Google Doc, references attached, teachers anonymised by construction.

57
00:03:48,743 --> 00:03:54,603
When a new round lands, one more button rewrites the analysis for it, machine checked before anyone can publish.

58
00:03:55,053 --> 00:03:55,990
Underneath, three locks.

59
00:03:55,990 --> 00:03:57,551
A password for the school.

60
00:03:57,551 --> 00:03:59,736
A second, server verified password for administrators.

61
00:03:59,736 --> 00:04:02,234
And a unique key for every single record.

62
00:04:02,234 --> 00:04:08,166
The whole system runs on the tools a school already pays for: Google Workspace, a database, and static hosting.

63
00:04:08,166 --> 00:04:13,474
No servers to maintain, no per seat licences, and the data stays in accounts the school controls.

64
00:04:13,924 --> 00:04:17,900
From a lesson observed, to evidence, to a plan in the teacher's hand.

65
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:20,653
One system, built inside a school, ready to travel.

66
00:04:20,653 --> 00:04:21,571
Better never stops.
